{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1541693-m20-base-successes-and-dividing-successes","id":1541693,"title":"[M20] Base Successes, and Dividing Successes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-07T11:58:11-07:00","id":1541693,"title":"[M20] Base Successes, and Dividing Successes","content":"I have a few questions regarding <i>Base Successes</i> and the Optional Rule &quot;<i>Dividing Successes</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#33AA33\">Question 1:</span></b> For now, let us put <i>Dividing Successes</i> aside, and focus on <i>Base Successes</i>.<br /> From the way that I managed to understand this, Effects always require a Base amount of Successes before they can take effect.<br /> Let us say that I would like to damage someone's patterns with Life magick, that means that I would need at least 2 <i>Base Successes</i>.<br /> Does that mean that in case I accumulated 3 successes with my Arete rolls, I would deal 6 Aggravated?<br /> Or alternatively, that would only be 2 Aggravated, because there is only one success above the <i>Base Successes</i>?<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#33AA33\"><b>Question 2:</b></span> When a Mage is <i>Dividing Successes</i>, from the way the book is describing it, it seem like the <i>Base Successes</i> are essentially <i>turning into</i> &quot;Additional Toll&quot;, as described on the bottom line of Question 1.<br /> Is that really the case? Meaning you must first accumulate the <i>Base Successes</i>, and only further successes will determine the systems of the Effect?<br /> Meaning if I wanted to affect two individuals with that Life magick I described on Question 1, that would require <i>2 Base Successes</i>, <i>1 Target Success</i>, and further successes that will got into Damage will deal 2 Damage each?<br /> Example: 5 Successes to deal 4 Aggravated to each of the two targets.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#33AA33\"><b>Question 3:</b></span> If I got everything correctly so far, well this section in the book does not make a lot of sense (page 564).<br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/dIE641L.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/dIE641L.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/dIE641L.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> So if we take a closer look, the book seem to greatly miscalculate the required successes to achieve the effect:<br /> <b>[Described Successes on the Book]</b><br /> <b>Base Successes:</b> 4<br /> <b>Six Targets:</b> 7? possibly 3.<br /> <b>One Story Duration:</b> 3<br /> <b>Correspondence:</b> 5<br /> <b>Total Successes Required according to the book:</b> 18<br /> <b>Total Successes Required if you actually count:</b> 19 or 15.....<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>[In reality?]</b><br /> <b>Base Successes:</b> 4<br /> <b>Six Targets:</b> 5<br /> <b>One Story Duration:</b> 3<br /> <b>Correspondence:</b> 5<br /> <b>Total Successes Required:</b> 17","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","user":"Lirbo","date":". 09-07-2024, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T13:24:20-07:00","id":1541698,"title":"","content":"Question 1<br /> <br /> There are 4 types of Arete rolls using Base Successes<br /> <br /> 1. All or nothing effects<br /> <br /> This includes things like teleporting, stepping sideways, triggering an explosion, etc. Things that either they work, or they don't. Here you need to get the full amount of successes or else nothing happens.<br /> <br /> 2. Impact based effects<br /> <br /> These tend to be things you see on the Magickal Feats table. Depending on how impressive you want your effect to be, you and your ST select how many successes you intend to go for. Then that is your goal. If you get half the successes needed then the ST may allow a partial effect, and if you get an excess of 3 successes to your goal, the ST may allow you to get a small bonus for it.<br /> <br /> 3. Damage based effects<br /> <br /> You roll your successes and see how much damage you do.<br /> <br /> 4. Duration based effects.<br /> <br /> You roll your successes and see how long the effect lasts for.<br /> <br /> For both Damage and Duration, you can instead choose a set amount of damage, or a set amount of duration to go for, this makes it become closer to an Impact based effect where you don't see how much you roll, but instead try to get the target number of successes required, and if you overshoot, that isn't more damage or more duration, but instead just succeeding at the effect (and if you get 3 above, then you could get a different bonus as decided by the ST)<br /> <br /> <br /> So damaging someone with Life, if you get 2 successes, then according to the table, that is 2 points of damage provided. If instead you got 3 successes it would instead by 6 damage<br /> <br /> <br /> Question 2<br /> The way divided successes works in M20 is based on a miscalculation of how it works in Revised.<br /> <br /> In revised, the based successes are the target, and once you achieve that target you are free to divide your success pool in to aspects of the effect.<br /> So, if your target to harm another person is 3, and you get 3 successes, then you can divide that between number of targets and amount of damage (so you could go 1 to affect other and 2 to damage to attack 1 target for 4 points of damage, or go 1 to affect other, 1 to get a second target, and 1 for damage to attack 2 targets for 2 points of damage each)<br /> <br /> Considering that M20 directly references Revised when it discusses Divided successes, I suspect the intent was to lift the system directly. But the author simply didn't understand the maths of it, and so made it needlessly expensive instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you wish to do divided successes, I highly recommend not using the miscalculated version that M20 provides.<br /> <br /> Question 3<br /> yes, this is another miscalculation (because why stop at one?)<br /> <br /> Author's can't math.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T06:52:55-07:00","id":1541859,"title":"","content":"I would bet the six targets for seven successes it's a typo. Since the base was already calculated at 4, the only way you would ever get a &quot;7 total&quot; would be if it was two targets per extra success - and then it would be 15 total. But it's one success per target elsewhere, isn't it?. If it's 6 instead of 7, you would get 18.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T09:57:28-07:00","id":1541874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1541693-m20-base-successes-and-dividing-successes#post1541693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So if we take a closer look, the book seem to greatly miscalculate the required successes to achieve the effect:<br /> <b>[Described Successes on the Book]</b><br /> <b>Base Successes:</b> 4<br /> <b>Six Targets:</b> 7? possibly 3.<br /> <b>One Story Duration:</b> 3<br /> <b>Correspondence:</b> 5<br /> <b>Total Successes Required according to the book:</b> 18<br /> <b>Total Successes Required if you actually count:</b> 19 or 15.....<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>[In reality?]</b><br /> <b>Base Successes:</b> 4<br /> <b>Six Targets:</b> 5<br /> <b>One Story Duration:</b> 3<br /> <b>Correspondence:</b> 5<br /> <b>Total Successes Required:</b> 17</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few other problems here, the Base Successes was calculated wrong as well. This effect is not a Control Minds spell, that takes Mind 3. By both Sphere rank and description, this is an Influence Minds spell. So the base successes is 3, not 4. Also, though this is an ST call, weeks of digging up dirt on someone could count for a better connection than &quot;Described Location.&quot; <br /> <br /> <b>Base Successes:</b> 3<br /> <b>Six Targets:</b> 5<br /> <b>One Story Duration:</b> 3<br /> <b>Correspondence:</b> 4<br /> <b>Total Successes Required:</b> 15","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}